# Audit96 A01–C11 exact observable assertions

> STAMP | artifact_version: v1.0.0 | scope: independent A01–C11 source-predicate expansion for PRD v7.3.4 | owner: `/root/audit96_abc` | source: `tasks/marketing-agent-v18-completeness-audit.output` v1.2.0
>
> Rule: every row has one observable happy path (H), one edge-state observation (E), and one failure/forbidden-action observation (F). These are source-row predicates, not aggregate coverage claims.

| ID | H: happy observable | E: edge observable | F: failure observable / forbidden action | source exact phrase |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A01 | Google CTA completes into first-login continuation | User cancels and stays on public login | Callback failure shows retry; no authenticated success shell | “Public login with Google CTA, cancel, callback failure, retry, and first-login continuation.” |
| A02 | No-invite first login creates one named workspace with owner role | Valid invite joins the named invited workspace with invited role | Cancel/failure creates no phantom workspace or membership | “First login creates or joins exactly one explicit tenant/workspace.” |
| A03 | Confirmed workspace switch changes active workspace and its role | Switch loading is visible before target data replaces current data | Failed/cancelled switch retains prior workspace; stale rows absent | “A multi-tenant user sees and deliberately switches the active workspace.” |
| A04 | Tenant A can read and mutate only A source/content/asset/account/job/metric records | A forbidden deep link returns an explicit safe denial | Tenant A search/select/API write against B produces no row, mutation, or external action | “One tenant can never see or mutate another tenant's sources, content, assets, accounts, jobs, or metrics.” |
| A05 | Customer, approver, and operator see their permitted actions | Consequential unavailable action is disabled/hidden with its reason | Forged role API request for approve/publish/credential/support is rejected | “Customer, approver, and operator roles see only authorized actions.” |
| A06 | Server-readback verified connection renders ready | Retry after a service fault keeps the safe local work | Timeout/401/403/500/callback mismatch never renders connected/ready | “Authentication/service failure never becomes a false-success shell.” |
| B01 | Existing non-GitHub wiki import confirms selected scope | Import preview shows source and chosen document scope | Fixture import count/scope/pointers/citations cannot report success unless usable | “A non-technical customer can import an existing wiki/brand source without GitHub.” |
| B02 | Retrieved selected repository files become evidence | Branch/path selection preview is shown before sync outcome | Public/private/bad URL/permission failure cannot show success before retrieval | “A customer can connect a GitHub repository and choose what becomes evidence.” |
| B03 | New wiki has title, template-or-blank choice, and first saved page | First-page save state is visible before reload | Failed save is not retrievable in Studio and tenant ownership is not created falsely | “A customer can create a new wiki inside the product when none exists.” |
| B04 | Confirmed fact edit is saved and used by next generation | Editor labels fact, inference, and unverified claim with citation/changed fields | Unverified value is blocked from generation/publication; save error remains recoverable | “A customer can edit wiki facts and distinguish fact, inference, and unverified claim.” |
| B05 | Supported generated claim shows its selected citation and evidence state | Inference claim renders its inference badge rather than confirmed | Unsupported claim has unverified/blocked state, not a fabricated citation | “Every generated claim exposes the selected source and evidence state.” |
| B06 | Manual sync records last successful time and source hash/version | Changed source updates retrieval; unchanged sync is idempotent | Stale/in-progress sync does not claim fresh truth | “A customer can manually sync the selected wiki/repo and see freshness.” |
| B07 | Last approved guide stays active after a sync fault | Permission/timeout/parse/deleted/partial failures offer retry or reconnect | Partial import never overwrites last-good version | “Sync failure preserves the last good version and gives a repair path.” |
| B08 | Sync history shows added/changed/removed facts with author/source/time | Customer can accept a reviewed change into a new active truth | Rejection keeps old approved facts active, including price/policy deletion diff | “A customer can inspect a sync diff/history before accepting changed brand truth.” |
| B09 | Approved wiki facts generate a guide draft with cited fields | Selected source scope progress and unsupported-field warning are visible | Guide draft cannot auto-approve or auto-activate | “The system can generate a draft brand guide from approved wiki facts.” |
| B10 | Structured guide edit saves and reloads positioning/audience/promise/proof/taboo/vocabulary | Validation names the invalid field without losing edits | Audit records editor actor and changed fields; unsaved change is not active | “A customer can edit the generated brand guide before use.” |
| B11 | v1/v2 guide versions are named, comparable, and old artifact remains v1-bound | Rollback creates v3 rather than changing v1/v2 | Archive/history operation cannot rewrite prior guide revision | “Brand guide revisions are immutable, named, and comparable.” |
| B12 | Human approval makes exactly one immutable guide snapshot active | Reject/request-change records actor and time | Forged activation of unapproved guide is denied | “A human explicitly approves the brand guide version used for generation.” |
| B13 | Artifact lineage names approved guide version and applied rules | After v2 approval, customer can choose regeneration under v2 | Existing v1 artifact does not silently switch to v2 | “Every content revision shows which approved brand-guide version was applied.” |
| B14 | Tone draft stores approved example sources/times/rationale, inferred anchors/sliders/phrases, and confidence | Selected examples produce traceable tone anchors | Insufficient examples become needs-review; active-tone mutation and confident-tone copy are forbidden | “Tone can be generated from approved examples without silently inventing a voice.” |
| B15 | Tone rule edit shows plain-language slider, do/don’t examples, and before/after preview | Save/error state permits rule correction without publishing | Preview/rule edit causes no external publication | “A customer can edit tone rules in customer language.” |
| B16 | Tone v1/v2 shows draft/approved/retired status, diff, approver, effective date | Metadata-only change preserves the current approval | Tone content change invalidates approval; raw slider state cannot bypass history | “Tone revisions have approval/version history independent of raw slider state.” |
| B17 | Generation-input panel identifies approved tone version and applied rules | Two tone versions on same source show inspectable output delta | Artifact cannot claim tone application without version stamp/rule binding | “The approved tone version is demonstrably applied to generation.” |
| C01 | Start campaign retains opportunity source URL/time/evidence and chosen rationale into brief/Studio | Customer can choose rationale before campaign creation | Missing source/cancel/duplicate/persistence failure creates no campaign or only named hold, never external action | “A customer can turn an opportunity/idea into a campaign rather than an untracked prompt.” |
| C02 | Campaign has a customer-language measurable goal visible in approval/result | Empty goal enters explicitly named exploratory mode if allowed | Missing goal cannot silently fan out generation | “A campaign has one explicit goal.” |
| C03 | Brief holds audience, offer, CTA, and key message | Changing one field updates variants while platform constraints remain distinct | Missing required brief field cannot become approved fan-out | “A campaign names audience, offer, desired action, and key message.” |
| C04 | Fresh campaign defaults to No paid spend and approval displays its budget disposition | Production cap is stored separately from informational paid-media budget | Entering cap/default state triggers no billing, ad, bid, or spend API | “Budget is explicit even when the product must not spend money.” |
| C05 | Campaign stores start/end/deadline/timezone and shows it in approval/Calendar | Cross-timezone schedule fit is evaluated | Past deadline or date conflict cannot silently schedule | “A campaign has a deadline/date window and timezone.” |
| C06 | Brief approved state records actor/time/version before fan-out | Change-requested and stale states are explicit | Changing goal/audience/offer/budget/deadline invalidates approval and dependent drafts | “The customer approves the campaign brief before content fan-out.” |
| C07 | Safety panel lists prohibited claim/topic and applicable crisis/legal/medical/financial warning | Review identifies the exact originating safety rule/source | Prohibited claim blocks generation/review until named repair | “Brand-safety rules and taboo topics are explicit, inspectable constraints.” |
| C08 | Claim checklist records claim/evidence/state/resolution | Adding approved proof changes only that exact claim | Unsupported price/guarantee cannot pass as fluent copy or unblock unrelated claims | “Risky claims require cited proof or customer correction, never fluent guessing.” |
| C09 | Photo/card-news/video asset inspector contains source, license/permission, territory, expiry, owner, proof | Valid rights pass preflight for the corresponding medium | Unknown/expired rights block approval, publish, and adapter call for all three media families | “Every photo/card-news/video asset has source and usage rights before approval.” |
| C10 | Person consent and AI disclosure are recorded with channel-specific preview/payload | Not-applicable disclosure/consent requires a reason | Person asset without consent cannot publish; required AI disclosure cannot be dropped | “Person consent and AI disclosure are recorded where applicable.” |
| C11 | One campaign’s canonical ID/brief/artifact/approval/job/result/learning links are clickable and traceable | A versioned campaign appears consistently across all projections | ID/version cannot silently change or orphan between idea, content, approval, job, result, and learning | “Campaign identity/version survives idea → content → approval → job → result → learning.” |

## Mechanical verification

- Row count: `A01..A06` = 6, `B01..B17` = 17, `C01..C11` = 11; total `34`.
- Each row has exactly one `H:`, one `E:`, and one `F:` assertion; total `102` observable assertions.
- IDs are unique and ordered A01–A06, B01–B17, C01–C11.
- No assertion relies on an aggregate count, `MATCH`, hash, or prior critic result.

## Self-question

**If this is wrong, why?** A source-row’s prose may combine a customer contract and a suggested test fixture. This artifact retains both only where they produce an observable UI, persistence, lineage, or forbidden-action assertion; it does not substitute broad `semantic mismatch0` language for an actual state transition or safety block.
